{
  "coreName": "Ikemen GO",
  "systemId": "IkemenGO",
  "systemNames": {
    "IkemenGO": "Ikemen GO"
  },
  "kind": "game",
  "author": "Ikemen GO contributors (ikemen-engine/Ikemen-GO; Suehiro, K4thos, NeatUnsou, ShinLucho, Daniel Porto, Gacel, Nikolay Griva and others); chimera core by Sergio Martin",
  "url": "https://github.com/ikemen-engine/Ikemen-GO",
  "romFile": "game",
  "extensions": {
    ".zip": "IkemenGO"
  },
  "_comment_extensions": "An Ikemen GO game is a folder (chars/, stages/, data/, save/...); the core opens it as one .zip of that folder.",
  "deterministic": true,
  "memoryLayoutMiB": [
    1024,
    16,
    16,
    16,
    6144
  ],
  "_memoryLayoutMiB_note": "sbrk, sealed, invisible, plain, mmap. Ikemen GO is a Go program: the Go runtime reserves about 1.4 GiB of address space at start (most of it never touched) and keeps its heap, the goroutines' stacks and what the game loads in mmap'd memory; Mesa's textures and buffers are there too. The game's zip is not copied in: it is read from the file Chimera mounted, an entry when it is opened.",
  "video": {
    "_comment": "What Ikemen GO draws with its OpenGL 3.3 renderer on the Mesa llvmpipe compiled into the core (made to generate the same code on every computer), read after each frame. The live size is the game's own resolution (GameWidth x GameHeight in its config); capacity here is the largest allowed.",
    "width": 1920,
    "height": 1080,
    "getBgra": "GetVideoBgra",
    "vsyncNumerator": 60,
    "vsyncDenominator": 1
  },
  "audio": {
    "_comment": "Ikemen GO's own mixer, mixed for exactly one frame's share of a second each frame: 735 stereo samples at 44100 Hz at 60 frames a second. samplesPerFrame is capacity.",
    "sampleRate": 44100,
    "channels": 2,
    "samplesPerFrame": 44100,
    "get": "GetAudio"
  },
  "lag": {
    "inputWasRead": "InputWasRead"
  },
  "settings": [
    {
      "name": "startTime",
      "display": "Starting Clock",
      "type": "int",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 2147483647,
      "default": 946684800,
      "description": "The date and time the game reads when it starts, in seconds since 1970 (Unix time), in UTC; it then runs with the frames, 1/60 of a second each. Ikemen GO also seeds its random numbers (a random stage, a random character, the AI's choices) from it as it starts. The default is the first of January 2000. This is a setting, and not your computer's clock, so that a movie plays back the same on any day. It is part of the machine, so a movie needs the same value."
    }
  ],
  "firmware": [],
  "input": {
    "name": "Ikemen GO",
    "_comment": "Four players, each a game controller in Ikemen GO's own default layout (its [Joystick_Pn] settings, which the core sets): the directions on the pad, A B X Y the face buttons, C the right trigger, Z the right shoulder, D the left shoulder, W the left trigger, Start, and Menu the Back button. Escape is the keyboard's, which leaves a menu or a match.",
